KEY Enter Opens the message.
KEY k QSL it: tells the sender you have it.
KEY x Marks it processed: you have acted on it.
KEY e Exports it to the export folder.
KEY M Shows only messages for this station.
KEY D Hides delivered messages.
KEY P Shows processed messages too.
KEY / Filters the list as you type.
SEE MSG-VIEW MSG-PENDING MSG-SEARCH
BEGIN_TEXT
Every message that came in, newest first. Columns: number, date-time
group, precedence, from, to, message id and state.

States: NEW (not opened), READ, QSL (receipt sent), PROC (processed),
DISC (discarded), DELIV (delivered on to its addressee).

Higher precedence comes first within a day: FLASH (Z), IMMEDIATE (O),
PRIORITY (P), ROUTINE (R). Each has a time to handle it in; a message
past its time shows in the status strip.
END
BEGIN_EXAMPLE
A PRIORITY message from NCS-A arrives at 1412Z. It shows at the top as
NEW. Enter opens it; k sends the QSL and the state becomes QSL. When you
have done what it asks, x marks it processed and it leaves the default
view (P shows it again).
END
